    "media:imagetext": "1928\nA CONSIDERABLY IMPROVED AND AERODYNAMICALLY CLEANER VERSION THAN\nTHE SIKORSKY S-36 WAS THE S-38, LAUNCHED IN 1928. IN ADDITION TO\nA CONSIDERABLE MAIL LOAD IT CARRIED NINE PASSENGERS OVER A RANGE OF\n600 MILES.\n600 MILES. THIS TWIN-ENGINE PLANE PIONEERED CARIBBEAN SERVICE.\nCOL.\nCHARLES A. LINDBERGH USED IT ON THE FIRST MIAMI-PANAMA SCHEDULED\nFLIGHT. THE TWO 420-HORSEPOWER ENGINES GAVE IT A CRUISING SPEED OF\n110 MILES-PER-HOUR\n110 MILES-PER-HOUR. FORTY-FEET, THREE-INCHES LONG, IT HAD A WING\nArnanCIA SPREAD OF 71-FEET,\nSPREAD OF 71-FEET, EIGHT-INCHES.",
